proof.text:
Fix $E\subset L$ and $H$. The assumed equality $\delta T(u^E_H)=u^L_{TH}\beta$ gives $S_L(\delta^{-1})S_L(u^L_{TH})=S_L(Tu^E_H)S_L(\beta^{-1})$. Naturality of $\varphi$ in [lem-weil-point-sections-scalar-extension] and the assumed inverse-image sections square therefore give
$$\begin{aligned}
\zeta_{L/E,H}v^L_{TH}
&=\varphi_{L/E,J_EH}S_L(Tu^E_H)S_L(\beta^{-1})\sigma^{g,L}_{TH}\\
&=(S_E(u^E_H)\otimes1)\varphi_{L/E,G_EH}S_L(\beta^{-1})\sigma^{g,L}_{TH}\\
&=(S_E(u^E_H)\otimes1)(\sigma^{g,E}_H\otimes1)\varphi_{L/E,H}
=(v^E_H\otimes1)\varphi_{L/E,H}.
\end{aligned}$$
This uses naturality of $\varphi$ at the single arrow $u^E_H$, not naturality of the family $u$.
